PSG: a noise table that does not overflow a signed int

MakeNoiseTable() shifts 32 bits into an int, one at a time, and the last of
them overflows it. Signed overflow is undefined behaviour, and
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer stops the program at it:

  src/chips/np2/fmgen_psg.cpp:75:11: runtime error: signed integer overflow:
  1207315479 * 2 cannot be represented in type 'int'

The shift register beside it has the same fault: it is shifted left by 16,
which leaves its highest bits outside an int as well.

Both are unsigned now. The table they fill is unsigned already
(PSG::noisetable), the values are never negative, and the numbers that come
out are the ones the code has always worked with.

This is ADLplug-Next's own patch, applied to the submodule by
cmake/Patches.cmake when CMake configures, and it goes away once the change is
upstream.

diff --git a/src/chips/np2/fmgen_psg.cpp b/src/chips/np2/fmgen_psg.cpp
index aa14588..cab1996 100644
--- a/src/chips/np2/fmgen_psg.cpp
+++ b/src/chips/np2/fmgen_psg.cpp
@@ -66,10 +66,10 @@ void PSG::MakeNoiseTable()
 {
 	if (!noisetable[0])
 	{
-		int noise = 14321;
+		uint noise = 14321;
 		for (int i=0; i<noisetablesize; i++)
 		{
-			int n = 0;
+			uint n = 0;
 			for (int j=0; j<32; j++)
 			{
 				n = n * 2 + (noise & 1);
